# Document every change

Documentation is part of the work, not a follow-up. If you add, remove, or modify code in this repo, update [`DOCS.md`](../../DOCS.md) **in the same change** before you consider the task done.

## Always

1. Add a **Changelog** row (today’s date + one line on what changed and why it matters).
2. Update the relevant **module / screen / workflow** section when behaviour, routes, or how-to-use steps change.
3. If you unlock a nav item in `renderer/lib/navigation.ts`, document that screen.
4. Remove items from **Coming soon** / **Other modules** when they become usable.
5. For IPC, schema, RBAC, or service changes, add a short architecture note and the code/IPC path.

## Includes (do not skip)

- New features and new files
- Bug fixes and behaviour changes
- UX/UI changes (tables, keyboard shortcuts, buttons, labels)
- Setup, seed, tests, and developer workflows that people need to run

Trivial formatting-only edits (whitespace, unused import) do not need a changelog row.

## Do not

- Leave the only explanation in chat.
- Ship an undocumented sidebar route or user-facing workflow.
- Treat a change as “too small” to document if a user or maintainer would notice it.
